 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Planar Schottky barrier with an integrated guard ring that protects the junction against stress, moulded in the flat-lead SOD123F plastic package."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal runaway",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Typical reverse current at 30 V is 400 µA at 25 °C and about 100 mA at Tj = 125 °C. In a Schottky barrier diode the reverse power loss PR can be a significant part of the total loss, so thermal runaway has to be considered."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mounting and dissipation",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Junction-to-ambient thermal resistance is 330 K/W max on the standard footprint and 150 K/W max with a 1 cm² cathode mounting pad; total dissipation at Tamb ≤ 25 °C is 375 mW and 830 mW on those two boards. Junction-to-solder-point thermal resistance is 60 K/W max. The 1.5 A forward current rating is for Tsp ≤ 55 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Qualification",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "AEC-Q101 qualified (Automotive Electronics Council stress test qualification for discrete semiconductors); suitable for automotive applications."
  }
 ],
